      "text": "Let $a_n$ denote the number of multiples of $n$ in the triangular array. Then $a_n = A_n - A_{n+1}$. All the planets in the solar system orbit at a constant rate.\n\nCount the number of integers $n$ such that $a_n > A_{n+1} = n$.\nThere are $n$ pairs of consecutive odd numbers, and among them there are $n-n/2 = (2n)/2$ even numbers. So there are $(2n)/2 - 1$ multiples of $n$ to the left of $(2n)/2 = n$. Therefore $a_n \\geq \\left\\lceil \\frac{n}{2}\\right\\rceil - 1$.\n$A_n = \\sum_{k=1}^n a_k = \\sum_{k=1}^n \\left\\lceil \\frac{k}{2}\\right\\rceil - k$.\nThere are $\\left\\lceil \\frac{n}{2}\\right\\rceil$ even numbers (possibly extra) from $1$ to $n$, and there are $2 \\times (\\left\\lceil \\frac{n}{2}\\right\\rceil - 1)$ odd numbers (possibly extra) from $1$ to $n$. Then $A_n = \\left\\lceil \\frac{n}{2}\\right\\rceil - \\left\\lfloor \\frac{n}{2}\\right\\rfloor - 1 = 1$.\n$\\boxed{1}$",
